WEBVTT

00:00:00.125 --> 00:00:02.669
Hey there.
We just added Galleries to Basecamp.

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:03.920
Let me show you how it works.

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:07.882
So galleries exist inside
any docs and files tool, and they work

00:00:07.882 --> 00:00:10.885
best when you've got a folder
full of images like this.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:12.679
Now normally you're squinting at tiny

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:16.641
thumbnails, you gotta click them
to go full screen for a closer look.

00:00:16.641 --> 00:00:20.812
But now if you flip this little switch,
it's going to go from List View

00:00:20.812 --> 00:00:26.401
to Grid View, and you get a nice
big gallery that's easy to sift through.

00:00:26.443 --> 00:00:28.236
You can click an image to make it full

00:00:28.236 --> 00:00:31.906
screen, cycle through the images
with the arrows just like before,

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:35.160
and then back on the grid, if you ever see
a number in the corner here,

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:38.121
that number just tells you
how many comments were made on that image.

00:00:38.121 --> 00:00:41.249
So click it and you can see
what the discussion is about.

00:00:41.791 --> 00:00:43.043
And check this out.

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:44.085
If you have a couple folders

00:00:44.085 --> 00:00:47.714
with images inside them, once
you're in that root folder,

00:00:47.964 --> 00:00:52.052
you can switch from list to Grid View
and you get a little mosaic

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:53.136
of what's in each folder.

00:00:53.136 --> 00:00:55.597
Just a peek
so you don't have to go inside.

00:00:55.597 --> 00:00:57.640
And then back in List View,

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:00.643
you can preview a folder
and you can switch to Grid View there.

00:01:01.519 --> 00:01:05.398
It's going to blow up the images you can
scan through without opening the folder.

00:01:05.523 --> 00:01:08.985
If I close it and open it again,
preview stays in Grid

00:01:09.152 --> 00:01:12.238
View and in fact so does
the folder itself.

00:01:12.322 --> 00:01:14.824
Right? So we go inside still in Grid View.

00:01:14.824 --> 00:01:17.327
And then back
here, just know that turning it on

00:01:17.327 --> 00:01:20.413
for this folder, it's
not going to turn it on for any others.

00:01:20.538 --> 00:01:24.459
And switching view modes doesn't change
anything for anyone else in your account.

00:01:24.459 --> 00:01:27.212
It's specific to your preferences.

00:01:27.212 --> 00:01:30.673
And heads up - this does work
with text documents as well.

00:01:30.965 --> 00:01:31.466
Really helps

00:01:31.466 --> 00:01:35.053
when you just want to peak in and see what
the first several lines are about.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:36.888
And last little fun thing -

00:01:36.888 --> 00:01:40.141
you can add a docs and files
tool to your project home page,

00:01:40.225 --> 00:01:43.645
drop a bunch of images in,
and then back on the project home page.

00:01:43.645 --> 00:01:46.648
You just get this lovely photo album
look to it.

00:01:46.648 --> 00:01:50.401
It's just a nice visual flavor
that instantly tells you what's in here.

00:01:50.401 --> 00:01:51.569
And that's it!

00:01:51.569 --> 00:01:54.989
Much better way to preview
images in Basecamp using Galleries.

00:01:54.989 --> 00:01:57.283
It's especially nice to use on your phone,
where

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:59.661
everything is
so much tinier than a computer screen.

00:01:59.661 --> 00:02:02.288
So hop in there and flip the switch.
